.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Passing quadrants and data to neighboring processes\&. 

See also the page \fBThe ghost layer\fP for general information\&. 
.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef struct \fBp4est_ghost\fP \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP"

.PP
Quadrants that neighbor the local domain\&. See also the page \fBThe ghost layer\fP for general information\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBp4est_locidx_t\fP p4est_face_quadrant_exists (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP treeid, const \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP * q, int * face, int * hang, int * owner_rank)"

.PP
Checks if quadrant exists in the local forest or the ghost layer\&. For quadrants across tree boundaries it checks if the quadrant exists across any face, but not across corners\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest in which to search for \fIq\fP\&. 
.br
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer in which to search for \fIq\fP\&. 
.br
\fItreeid\fP The tree to which \fIq\fP belongs\&. 
.br
\fIq\fP The quadrant that is being searched for\&. 
.br
\fIface\fP On input, face id across which \fIq\fP was created\&. On output, the neighbor's face number augmented by orientation, so face is in 0\&.\&.7\&. 
.br
\fIhang\fP If not NULL, signals that q is bigger than the quadrant it came from\&. The child id of that originating quadrant is passed into hang\&. On output, hang holds the hanging face number of \fIq\fP that is in contact with its originator\&. 
.br
\fIowner_rank\fP Filled with the rank of the owner if it is found and undefined otherwise\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns the local number of \fIq\fP if the quadrant exists in the local forest or in the ghost_layer\&. Otherwise, returns -2 for a domain boundary and -1 if not found\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "ssize_t p4est_ghost_bsearch (\fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, int which_proc, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, const \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP * q)"

.PP
Conduct binary search for exact match on a range of the ghost layer\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_proc\fP The owner of the searched quadrant\&. Can be -1\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP The tree of the searched quadrant\&. Can be -1\&. 
.br
\fIq\fP Valid quadrant is searched in the ghost layer\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Offset in the ghost layer, or -1 if not found\&. 
.RE
.PP

