.SS "void p4est_ghost_exchange_custom (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, size_t data_size, void ** mirror_data, void * ghost_data)"

.PP
Transfer data for local quadrants that are ghosts to other processors\&. The data size is the same for all quadrants and can be chosen arbitrarily\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP The data size to transfer per quadrant\&. 
.br
\fImirror_data\fP One data pointer per mirror quadrant as input\&. 
.br
\fIghost_data\fP Pre-allocated contiguous data for all ghosts in sequence, which must hold at least \fCdata_size\fP for each ghost\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_ghost_exchange_t\fP* p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_begin (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, size_t data_size, void ** mirror_data, void * ghost_data)"

.PP
Begin an asynchronous ghost data exchange by posting messages\&. The arguments are identical to p4est_ghost_exchange_custom\&. The return type is always non-NULL and must be passed to p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_end to complete the exchange\&. The ghost data must not be accessed before completion\&. The mirror data can be safely discarded right after this function returns since it is copied into internal send buffers\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP The data size to transfer per quadrant\&. 
.br
\fImirror_data\fP Not required to stay alive any longer\&. 
.br
\fIghost_data\fP Must stay alive into the completion call\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Transient storage for messages in progress\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_end (\fBp4est_ghost_exchange_t\fP * exc)"

.PP
Complete an asynchronous ghost data exchange\&. This function waits for all pending MPI communications\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIexc\fP created ONLY by p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_begin\&. It is deallocated before this function returns\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_levels (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, int minlevel, int maxlevel, size_t data_size, void ** mirror_data, void * ghost_data)"

.PP
Transfer data for local quadrants that are ghosts to other processors\&. The data size is the same for all quadrants and can be chosen arbitrarily\&. This function restricts the transfer to a range of refinement levels\&. The memory for quadrants outside the level range is not dereferenced\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer used for reference\&. 
.br
\fIminlevel\fP Level of the largest quads to be exchanged\&. Use <= 0 for no restriction\&. 
.br
\fImaxlevel\fP Level of the smallest quads to be exchanged\&. Use >= P4EST_QMAXLEVEL for no restriction\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP The data size to transfer per quadrant\&. 
.br
\fImirror_data\fP One data pointer per mirror quadrant as input\&. 
.br
\fIghost_data\fP Pre-allocated contiguous data for all ghosts in sequence, which must hold at least \fCdata_size\fP for each ghost\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_ghost_exchange_t\fP* p4est_ghost_exchange_custom_levels_begin (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, int minlevel, int maxlevel, size_t data_size, void ** mirror_data, void * ghost_data)"

