.SS "\fBp4est_ghost_t\fP* p4est_ghost_new (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP btype)"

.PP
Builds the ghost layer\&. This will gather the quadrants from each neighboring proc to build one layer of face and corner based ghost elements around the ones they own\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest for which the ghost layer will be generated\&. 
.br
\fIbtype\fP Which ghosts to include (across face, corner or full)\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A fully initialized ghost layer\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBsteps/p4est_step3\&.c\fP, and \fBtimings/timings2\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "\fBp4est_ghost_t\fP* p4est_ghost_new_local (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP ctype)"

.PP
Generate an empty ghost layer\&. This ghost layer pretends that there are no parallel neighbor elements\&. It is useful if general algorithms should be run with local data only\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP Valid forest\&. 
.br
\fIctype\fP Ghosts to include (none, across face, face/corner)\&. This variable must be valid but has no effect\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Valid ghost layer of zero ghost elements\&. 
.RE
.PP

