.SS "int p4est_quadrant_exists (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_ghost_t\fP * ghost, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP treeid, const \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP * q, sc_array_t * exists_arr, sc_array_t * rproc_arr, sc_array_t * rquad_arr)"

.PP
Checks if quadrant exists in the local forest or the ghost layer\&. For quadrants across tree corners it checks if the quadrant exists in any of the corner neighbors, thus it can execute multiple queries\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest in which to search for \fIq\fP 
.br
\fIghost\fP The ghost layer in which to search for \fIq\fP 
.br
\fItreeid\fP The tree to which \fIq\fP belongs (can be extended)\&. 
.br
\fIq\fP The quadrant that is being searched for\&. 
.br
\fIexists_arr\fP Must exist and be of of elem_size = sizeof (int) for inter-tree corner cases\&. Is resized by this function to one entry for each corner search and set to true/false depending on its existence in the local forest or ghost_layer\&. 
.br
\fIrproc_arr\fP If not NULL is filled with one rank per query\&. 
.br
\fIrquad_arr\fP If not NULL is filled with one quadrant per query\&. Its piggy3 member is defined as well\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the quadrant exists in the local forest or in the ghost_layer, and false if doesn't exist in either\&. 
.RE
.PP

